Upstream model code
=========================================================================

--- mit (MIT License) ---

  acestep.cpp
    https://github.com/ServeurpersoCom/acestep.cpp
    Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The acestep.cpp authors

    Most of the C++ inference path under src/acestep/ is ported from this
    project's ggml implementation rather than written against the PyTorch
    reference directly:

      src/acestep/philox.h              from src/philox.h (verbatim)
      src/acestep/lm_pipeline.{h,cpp}   from src/sampling.h (sample_top_k_p,
                                        verbatim), src/prompt.h, pipeline-lm
      src/acestep/bpe_tokenizer.{h,cpp} from src/bpe.h
      src/acestep/metadata_fsm.h        from src/metadata-fsm.h
      src/acestep/lm_ggml.{h,cpp}       from src/qwen3-lm.h
      src/acestep/textenc_ggml.cpp      from src/qwen3-enc.h
      src/acestep/cond_ggml.{h,cpp}     from src/cond-enc.h
      src/acestep/detok_ggml.{h,cpp}    from src/fsq-detok.h
      src/acestep/dit_ggml.{h,cpp}      from src/dit-graph.h and src/dit*.h

    The stage GGUFs this engine loads are produced by that project's
    convert.py, and src/acestep/engine.cpp follows its pipeline wiring and
    LM sampling defaults so the two implementations can be compared tensor
    by tensor.

--- mit (MIT License) ---

  ACE-Step 1.5 (model architecture and weights)
    https://github.com/ace-step/ACE-Step-1.5
    The 5 Hz LM, FSQ detokenizer, DiT flow-matching transformer, and Oobleck
    VAE stages implement the ACE-Step 1.5 architecture; the weights are ACE
    Studio's and StepFun's. Note that the ACE-Step 1.5 line is MIT-licensed,
    unlike the Apache-2.0 ACE-Step v1 line; consult the LICENSE file of the
    specific upstream repository and the model card of the specific
    checkpoint being converted.

--- apache-2.0 (Apache License 2.0) ---

  Qwen3-Embedding (text-encoder stage)
    https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B
    The text-encoder stage runs Qwen3-Embedding weights, and the LM stage
    reuses the Qwen3 causal architecture (src/acestep/qwen3_block.h). The LM
    weights themselves ship with ACE-Step 1.5 and follow that project's
    license.

